        <groundspeak:log id="681185668">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 201 - Turner Valley (Replacement)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out doing some other caching today and since the unfortunate decision made by Geocaching.com, I figured I'd hurry up and get some of the caps I have remaining to find before I can't quite log them the same anymore. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_dissapprove.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_sad.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;  This was along the way, so I had my awesome driver friend (One Bad Ant) stop and let me get the right pictures. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;  Not sure if she'll log it, but I have the photos to say we were there. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;  TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="677221660">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-13T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1151545">Ringrat</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP201 Turner Valley Replacement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As dusk was falling I made another stop in Black Diamond for a cap. This one was in better shape than the last, though not perfect.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="642369646">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-09-17T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7364793">NurseB33</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP201 Turner Valley &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gate Keeper and I headed south for just a few hours to grab the new caches and realized we both didn't have the brass caps in this area. Naturally, we stopped to gather the required information before continuing on. Details have been sent to the C.O. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While looking for the cap an adorable boy, about 7 years old, rode by on his bicycle. Curiosity got the best of him and he headed over in our direction. He stretched out his little arm to shake mine and announced &quot;hi, my name is xxxxx, whatya looking for&quot;?  He was absolutely adorable... acting so mature yet clearly so young. Then he continued on to tell us about his phone and his sister's phone, and sorta rambled on like little boys do until he announced he should head home. That interaction put a smile on my face... kids are so refreshing, aren't they?!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks, OFTH for the brass cap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
